[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] voice_adherence: 7 -- The chapter largely maintains Elisa's voice well — the technical precision, the equation-murmuring, the granito tactile anchor. But in the final paragraphs, the prose drifts into a more generic literary register with symmetrical lists and on-the-nose metaphors ('buraco negro que não se vê'). Elisa's metaphors should come from physics, not from poetry. The voice profile explicitly states her domínio metafórico is 'física e termodinâmica.'
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] beat_coverage: 7 -- All five outline beats are present. The corporate meeting is well-dramatized with distinct voices. Renan's article is handled with appropriate devastation. The insomnia escalation is visceral. The lake scene is atmospheric. But the letter beat, while emotionally powerful, lacks the scene-work that the other beats receive — it's the most 'told' of the five.
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] character_voice: 7 -- Elisa's voice in dialogue is strong — 'Estou a pensar. É por isso que esto a investigar' is perfectly in character. Marcus's dialogue ('Dormir é o único tempo em que o cérebro processa o que aprendeu') captures his rapid, physics-metaphor style. The corporate meeting dialogue is the weakest section because the representatives are more functional than real.
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] plants_seeded: 8 -- The chapter plants several elements naturally: the letter in Portuguese (personal threat), the mother's unfinished equation (deepest wound), the Nexion calibration data (scientific thread), Marcus preparing something in preprint (betrayal/alliance ambiguity), and the CERN parallel (structural echo). All are integrated into scene work rather than dropped in.
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] prose_quality: 6 -- The prose is strongest in concrete, specific moments — the granito's thumb-polish, the three coffee mugs in a semicircle, Marcus's four-day beard, the neon-lit wet asphalt. It weakens when it summarizes emotional states ('O mundo apertava') or uses symmetrical list structures. The chapter has several passages where consecutive sentences start with the same structure ('Elisa...' 'Elisa...' 'Elisa...'), creating rhythmic monotony. The strongest writing is in the insomnia scene with Marcus — the physical details are sharp and the dialogue crackles.
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] continuity: 8 -- The chapter follows logically from Chapter 13. Elisa's emotional state tracks — she's moving from the existential confrontation with Helena (Chapter 13's lake scene) into the external pressure phase. The insomnia escalation is a natural consequence of the previous chapter's emotional weight. The corporate meeting, Renan's article, and the letter all represent the 'bad guys closing in' beat appropriately. The granito, the mother's watch, the USB drive — all continuity threads are maintained. One small note: the previous chapter ended with Elisa walking back from the lake toward the ETH, and this chapter opens in the ETH meeting room. The transition is clean but could benefit from a brief temporal marker — how much time has passed?
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] canon_compliance: 7 -- No major canon violations. The chapter is faithful to established facts, character descriptions, and world rules. The closest thing to a violation is the letter's knowledge of the napkins, but this is clearly intended as a mystery/plot driver rather than an error.
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] lore_integration: 7 -- The chapter integrates the IC system, the Drakon unit, the calibration margins, the corporate structure (Nexion/Tianzi/Evromind), and the CERN data thread. The world is doing work. But the corporate meeting scene is the weakest in this dimension — it's the most 'generic thriller' moment in the chapter.
[2026-06-01 09:45:21] [SUBPROCESS] engagement: 7 -- The chapter earns its tension through accumulation rather than surprise — each beat adds pressure, and the reader feels the walls closing in. The letter scene is the most engaging moment because it's genuinely unexpected and personally devastating. The insomnia scene with Marcus provides human warmth that contrasts effectively with the corporate coldness. The chapter would score higher if it contained a moment that truly surprises — something the outline didn't predict and the reader doesn't see coming.
